Z||000000||GoCartGuy||04-14-2001||06:09 PM||||Well guys the interior is basically done, just gotta do a repaint on the plastics for the consoles but here's a link to the pics I've got scanned.  I haven't had a chance to get the other developed yet.<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1644181&a=12582313&f=0&vt=vp" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1644181&a=12582313&f=0&vt=vp</A> <P>Let me know what you think of if you got questions<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||10
Z||000001||Jay||04-14-2001||08:43 PM||||Looks good! I like the blue!!  One problem though, I had my glove box arm rest painted and after a while it didn't look painted anymore.  I used the interior paint stuff, but it still rubbed off.  You may want to consider wraping it in leather or vinyl.  I did mine in leather and just painted the glove box door.  It has held up for three years now, like new.  Look forward to seeing more.||||reg||10
Z||000002||Bluebottlejunky||04-14-2001||09:02 PM||||That is gunna look sweet man!  I used some vinal paint on my interior and it dose rub off...but oh well just repaint it.  Sence my interior is all black and red I need to figure out what to do about the grey seatbelts! l8ter <P>------------------<BR>BBJ<BR>85' GT 4sp<p>[This message has been edited by Bluebottlejunky (edited 04-14-2001).]||||reg||1
