Z||000006||GoCartGuy||04-15-2001||08:13 PM||||Well I finished it last night just as it started to rain, so no pics as of yet, should have them up by the end of the week though.  Thanks for all the input and to those of you repainting your interior have a little hint.  On the plastic trim pieces around the door make sure you put a coat or two of clear protector (acrylic or laquer) on them or they'll scratch kinda easy.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000007||fyerstarter||04-16-2001||01:01 PM||||Looking good can't wait to see it completed. And we both know the Fiero interior can use any help it can get  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Oh I do have a question for you, What did you use to repair your dash corners? Just a vinyl repair kit from the autoparts store or...?||||reg||1
Z||000008||GoCartGuy||04-17-2001||08:12 AM||||Ok hoping to take the pics when I get home from work tonight.  <P>In response to the last question.  I used Napa's Flex Bumper repair kit, its basically plastic in an epoxy form.  Works great and with a little homage to the Dremel god you can shape it into the corner, or as I found out the backing for those little holes in the plasic surrounds the we always tear the torx screws through.  Hey it also works great for repairing a cracked monitor case.  Just finding more and more cool uses for the stuff.  Its so much fun I might take up sculpture now.<P><P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
